 "conditionalInference": "All registered estimands, bootstrap intervals, multiplicity corrections, materiality tests and the catastrophe / false-selection vetoes are computed on accepted worlds only, i.e. they are conditional on the valid-menu population (and, as before, on the V3 validator, terminal, task and prior-world gates). Rejected worlds are counted in admission and never replaced; cell weights stay fixed, so a rejected world reduces its own cell only.",
 "generalizationLimitation": "Claims do not extend to worlds whose native menu presents one action twice. Under the frozen Forge World V2 generator this subpopulation exists only where a restore objective re-adds an existing dependency edge AND that edge carries an offered BYPASS (substitute-bearing roles, i.e. OOD_ROLES): observed 1/1,824 spent OOD_ROLES worlds (95% CP upper 0.0031), 0 elsewhere. Separately, 222/9,456 spent worlds (2.35%) present a duplicated dependency relationship in the observation without any menu effect; that is native generator behaviour present in every earlier stage, is not a menu defect, and is neither rejected nor repaired.",
 "verdict": "STATISTICAL_VALIDITY_NOT_ESTABLISHED",
 "authority": "R0"
